
# to create repository go to git hub and make a new repositorie
and copy the "url"

  # add all the local files to remote repo 

  :- git add remote origin URL

  # PUSH  (if you have modified the files in locally, you need to push them to remote "github")
 

   :- git push origin main

  # if you wanted push the files to branches 
   :- git push origin <branch name>
 
 # PULL (if you have modified the files in remote, you need to pull them locally git pull means "git fetch + git mergr")

 WHEN YOU RUN "git pull origin main" IT FIRST FETCH THE COMMITS IN REMOTE REPO AND MERGE THEM LOCALLY
 
 :git pull origin main

 :git pull origin --rebase 
  
